<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 17:27:41 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>🔴Germany’s far-right AfD landslide winner in key Saxony-Anhalt vote, early results suggest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-afd-could-lead-the-first-far-right-state-government-since-the-dark-days-of-nazism</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">7ed1d02e-aa0e-11f1-85ec-1dee8a48d84d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 16:18:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany’s far-right AfD landslide winner in key Saxony-Anhalt vote, early results suggest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-takes-huge-lead-in-key-vote-early-results-suggest</link><description>
Germany’s far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party headed towards a landslide victory in state ​elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday, with 44.5 percent of the vote, early results showed. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/727d2c16-aa12-11f1-ac8b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249584038776-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/727d2c16-aa12-11f1-ac8b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249584038776-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f25a936a-aa0d-11f1-81e7-1dee8a48d84d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 16:15:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/727d2c16-aa12-11f1-ac8b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249584038776-1.jpg">© Michael Kappeler, DPA via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>AfD could lead "the first far-right state government since the dark days of Nazism"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-afd-could-lead-the-first-far-right-state-government-since-the-dark-days-of-nazism</link><description>
Voting is underway in the eastern German state of Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday in a closely watched election. "If the AfD does form a government in Saxony-Anhalt, that would make it the first regional government headed by a far-right party since the end of the Second World War, since the dark days of Nazism", our correspondent Nick Holdsworth explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58b672fa-aa09-11f1-85c4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-170305-170528-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58b672fa-aa09-11f1-85c4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-170305-170528-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5d4f5ff2-aa09-11f1-96e8-0b904ca2da0a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 16:07:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Deauville Film Festival: What’s your favourite American film?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-deauville-film-festival-what-s-your-favourite-american-film</link><description>
The United States ranks second in the world in terms of the number of films produced. It produces between 500 and 700 films every year, which is just behind India. The Deauville Film Festival, with its stars, premieres and awards, aims to showcase the very best of what’s being made across the Atlantic. But on the other side of the screen, moviegoers also have their say. What’s your favourite American film? Is it one that shaped your childhood, or a recent discovery? Our reporter Gaëlle Fonseca hit the streets of Deauville to ask that very question.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e7dfacc-aa09-11f1-a7ff-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-vox-en.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e7dfacc-aa09-11f1-a7ff-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-vox-en.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">208b8c28-aa07-11f1-b6ea-4b32d2459595</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 15:43:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany: What could change in Saxony-Anhalt if the AfD wins?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-what-could-change-in-saxony-anhalt-if-the-afd-wins</link><description>
Voting began in the eastern German state of Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday in a closely watched election. Recent surveys place the AfD at just over 40%, followed by Merz's Christian Democrats (CDU) at 23%. If the AfD wins, "one of the main things they want to change is the education system. They say they want to reset education," our journalist Shirli Stibon explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/800c75ea-a9fd-11f1-bd6c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-160530-160948-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/800c75ea-a9fd-11f1-bd6c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-160530-160948-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">848fcc52-a9fd-11f1-9fe3-7780686f9d70</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 14:44:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>The week in pictures: Nepal rescue operations, World Nomad Games and Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260906-the-week-in-pictures-nepal-rescue-operations-world-nomad-games-and-russian-strikes-on-kyiv</link><description>
From the desperate search for workers trapped in the hydropower tunnels buried by the catastrophic flooding in Nepal to crowds of women mourning the victims of a US bombardment of a wedding in southern Iran, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce71f470-a846-11f1-aeb1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T042916Z-1913369404-RC22CNA80I6M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce71f470-a846-11f1-aeb1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T042916Z-1913369404-RC22CNA80I6M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dea2950c-a9bd-11f1-b557-b7773d79cef0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 14:21:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce71f470-a846-11f1-aeb1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T042916Z-1913369404-RC22CNA80I6M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg">© Athit Perawongmetha, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany: AfD's Ulrich Siegmund eyes outright majority</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-afd-s-ulrich-siegmund-eyes-outright-majority</link><description>
Under its 35-year-old lead ​candidate Ulrich Siegmund, the ‌AfD has polled above 40% for months and has a realistic shot at winning an absolute majority if several smaller parties fail ⁠to clear Germany's 5% hurdle to enter parliament.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1df5ea6-a9f7-11f1-826c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-150731-150908-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1df5ea6-a9f7-11f1-826c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-150731-150908-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d65ef45a-a9f7-11f1-b500-4b470eedca1a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 14:07:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine-Russia talks: What are the US objectives?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-ukraine-russia-talks-what-are-the-us-objectives</link><description>
US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner arrived in Kyiv on Sunday in their first official visit to Ukraine as part of a renewed push for peace, more than 4½ years after Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine. We discuss this topic with our guest, John E. Herbst, director of the Eurasia Center at the Atlantic Council.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebfe2368-a9f6-11f1-a121-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-140051-140759-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebfe2368-a9f6-11f1-a121-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-140051-140759-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f0bf7ffa-a9f6-11f1-9109-4b470eedca1a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 14:03:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Egyptian TV presenter Sarah Khalifa sentenced to death in drug case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260906-egyptian-tv-presenter-sarah-khalifa-sentenced-to-death-in-drug-case</link><description>
Sarah Khalifa, a well-known Egyptian TV presenter, has been sentenced to death for her involvement in a drug ring, state media reported over the weekend. Eleven others were also convicted in the case and handed a death sentence. Khalifa is best known for her program “Mission Impossible”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc9ddf20-a9f4-11f1-8ad4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-%C3%A9cran-2026-09-06-144741.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc9ddf20-a9f4-11f1-8ad4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-%C3%A9cran-2026-09-06-144741.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3415f0da-a9f8-11f1-bf5c-9b447c8e7aa4</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 13:52:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc9ddf20-a9f4-11f1-8ad4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-%C3%A9cran-2026-09-06-144741.jpg">© Sarah Khalifa, Instagram</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>AI: The future of smart households?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-ai-the-future-of-smart-households</link><description>
Could artificial intelligence soon be running our households? Beyond our smartphones, AI is now powering everything from fridges to lawnmowers. The International Household Appliances Fair in Berlin gives us a glimpse into what's next.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a6628692-a9f5-11f1-b510-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-132504-132632-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a6628692-a9f5-11f1-b510-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-132504-132632-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ab47e67a-a9f5-11f1-8265-4b470eedca1a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 13:50:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany: Why is the AfD so popular in Saxony-Anhalt?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-why-is-the-afd-so-popular-in-saxony-anhalt</link><description>
Voting began in the eastern German state of Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday in a closely watched election that could see the Alternative for Germany (AfD) become the first far-right party to lead a state government since World War II. We discuss this with our guest, Hans Stark, professor of German studies at Sorbonne University.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dfacf952-a9f3-11f1-a626-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-131541-132235-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dfacf952-a9f3-11f1-a626-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-131541-132235-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4ccfc48-a9f3-11f1-91bc-9b447c8e7aa4</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 13:37:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Indonesia's Anak Krakatau eruption halts flights, schools, fishing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-indonesia-s-anak-krakatau-eruption-halts-flights-schools-fishing</link><description>
An eruption of Indonesia's Mount Anak Krakatau caused six airports to suspend flight operations on Sunday, affecting hundreds of flights at Jakarta's main airport, after some school activities and fishing were halted.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a51d103e-a9e8-11f1-b319-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-120902-121027-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a51d103e-a9e8-11f1-b319-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-120902-121027-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a9fc524a-a9e8-11f1-aa6d-61eee6b21de8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 12:54:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Commemoration held for late Bosnian Serb war criminal Ratko Mladic</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-commemoration-held-for-late-bosnian-serb-war-criminal-ratko-mladic</link><description>
A commemoration was held Saturday in Belgrade for war criminal Ratko Mladic two days ahead of his burial, attended by dozens of former military personnel, family members and officials.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4695da0-a9e8-11f1-9f53-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-121051-121239-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4695da0-a9e8-11f1-9f53-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260906-121051-121239-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9406012-a9e8-11f1-8955-61eee6b21de8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 12:52:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany's far-right AfD clear frontrunner in eastern state vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-germany-s-far-right-afd-clear-frontrunner-in-eastern-state-vote-1</link><description>
German voters headed to the polls on Sunday for a key regional election in the ex-communist east where the far-right, anti-immigrant, Moscow- and Trump-friendly AfD is expected to secure an easy majority. Our correspondent Nick Holdsworth tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ded9a6e-a9bb-11f1-936f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7FD9V7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ded9a6e-a9bb-11f1-936f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7FD9V7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">957595b6-a9e8-11f1-b127-791dea6d5b8b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 11:54:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethan Hawke receives the Deauville Talent Award</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-ethan-hawke-receives-the-deauville-talent-award</link><description>
Known for starring in Dead Poets Society, the Before trilogy and Boyhood, Hollywood legend Ethan Hawke receives the #Deauville #Talent #Award in recognition of his career spanning nearly 40 years.
 
He also plays the lead role in The Weight, screened at the Opening Ceremony of the 52nd Deauville #American #Film #Festival and due to be released in theaters on September 16. Our reporter Gaëlle Fonseca spoke to him on the red carpet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c899b634-a9e8-11f1-b153-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/SUJET-VOX-POPS-00-11-27-23-Still003.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c899b634-a9e8-11f1-b153-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/SUJET-VOX-POPS-00-11-27-23-Still003.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f54c4b2-a9e7-11f1-a7d9-791dea6d5b8b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 11:49:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Army Secretary Dan Driscoll quits: "What we've seen is almost a factional clash"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260906-us-army-secretary-dan-driscoll-quits-what-we-ve-seen-is-almost-a-factional-clash</link><description>
